  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"1250\" data-end=\"1371\">\n<p data-start=\"1252\" data-end=\"1371\"><strong data-start=\"1252\" data-end=\"1272\">Normal response:</strong> TSH rises at least 2&ndash;5 times baseline by 20 minutes, then returns toward baseline by 60 minutes.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1372\" data-end=\"1502\">\n<p data-start=\"1374\" data-end=\"1502\"><strong data-start=\"1374\" data-end=\"1409\">Blunted or absent TSH response:</strong> May indicate secondary or tertiary hypothyroidism (pituitary or hypothalamic dysfunction).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1503\" data-end=\"1594\">\n<p data-start=\"1505\" data-end=\"1594\"><strong data-start=\"1505\" data-end=\"1534\">Exaggerated TSH response:</strong> Possible hypothyroidism or resistance to thyroid hormone.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
